    <Event name="onClick" paragraph="BTN-KBFOLDER--ONCLICK"><![CDATA[       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.

       DATA DIVISION.

       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
           *>   The Knowledge Base folder in its own dialog; the summary is read again after.

           INVOKE    ME::OpenFormSync("KB-FOLDER-FORM")

           *> PC-REFRESH: brings the summaries of the pane up to date: the Knowledge Base folder,
           *> the model list and what each of the four group buttons holds.
           *> Uses:   the setting KB-LOCATION, which the Knowledge Base folder dialog
           *>         (KB-FOLDER-FORM, modal, closed just above) may have just saved, and the
           *>         connections and agents as before. It also reads the application's model list
           *>         and the key store.
           *> Result: It also asks CHAT-FORM, with INVOKE super::"PC-REFRESH"(), to run its own
           *>         PC-REFRESH (fire-and-forget: the chat runs it when its event loop is next
           *>         idle), so the chat follows the change. Lbl-KbSum::Caption = the folder now
           *>         saved ("assets/KB" if none), which the chat takes over as its Knowledge Base
           *>         location; the other summaries and Lst-Models are rebuilt as well. MODELS-FILE
           *>         is first mirrored from the application's model list (PC-SYNC-MODELS): records
           *>         may be added, updated or deleted.

           CALL    "PC-REFRESH"
]]></Event>
  </Control>
