    <Event name="onClick" paragraph="BTN-PROVIDERS--ONCLICK"><![CDATA[       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.

       DATA DIVISION.

       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
           *>   The connections: provider, address and key in its own dialog; the summary is read again after.

           INVOKE    ME::OpenFormSync("PROVIDERS-FORM")

           *> PC-REFRESH: brings the summaries of the pane up to date: the Knowledge Base folder,
           *> the model list and what each of the four group buttons holds.
           *> Uses:   the connections in MODELS-FILE, which the Model providers dialog
           *>         (PROVIDERS-FORM, modal, closed just above) may have added, changed or deleted,
           *>         and the agent settings it clears for a deleted connection. It also reads the
           *>         application's model list and the key store.
           *> Result: It also asks CHAT-FORM, with INVOKE super::"PC-REFRESH"(), to run its own
           *>         PC-REFRESH (fire-and-forget: the chat runs it when its event loop is next
           *>         idle), so the chat follows the change. Lst-Models, Lbl-ProvSum, Lbl-ModelSum
           *>         and Lbl-AgentSum show the connections as they are now; Btn-ModelSel and
           *>         Btn-Agents are enabled only while at least one connection exists. MODELS-FILE
           *>         is first mirrored from the application's model list (PC-SYNC-MODELS): records
           *>         may be added, updated or deleted.

           CALL    "PC-REFRESH"
]]></Event>
  </Control>
