    <Event name="onClick" paragraph="BTN-MODELSEL--ONCLICK"><![CDATA[       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.

       DATA DIVISION.

       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
           *>   Each connection's model, rank and tools, in its own dialog. Only
           *>   once a provider is set up: the button is off until then.

           IF    WS-MODEL-COUNT = 0
               SET     Lbl-Status::Caption       TO    T-SUM-NEED-PROVIDER::Trim()
               EXIT PROGRAM
           END-IF
           INVOKE    ME::OpenFormSync("MODEL-FORM")

           *> PC-REFRESH: brings the summaries of the pane up to date: the Knowledge Base folder,
           *> the model list and what each of the four group buttons holds.
           *> Uses:   the model, rank and tools flag that the Model selection dialog (MODEL-FORM,
           *>         modal, closed just above) may have saved onto a connection in MODELS-FILE. It
           *>         also reads the application's model list and the key store.
           *> Result: It also asks CHAT-FORM, with INVOKE super::"PC-REFRESH"(), to run its own
           *>         PC-REFRESH (fire-and-forget: the chat runs it when its event loop is next
           *>         idle), so the chat follows the change. Lst-Models rows show the new model,
           *>         rank and tools tag; Lbl-ModelSum = how many connections now have a model; the
           *>         other summaries are rebuilt too. MODELS-FILE is first mirrored from the
           *>         application's model list (PC-SYNC-MODELS): records may be added, updated or
           *>         deleted.

           CALL    "PC-REFRESH"
]]></Event>
  </Control>
