    <Event name="onClick" paragraph="BTN-AGENTS--ONCLICK"><![CDATA[       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.

       DATA DIVISION.

       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
           *>   Which connection each of the chat's three agents uses, in its own
           *>   dialog. Only once a provider is set up.

           IF    WS-MODEL-COUNT = 0
               SET     Lbl-Status::Caption       TO    T-SUM-NEED-PROVIDER::Trim()
               EXIT PROGRAM
           END-IF
           INVOKE    ME::OpenFormSync("AGENTS-FORM")

           *> PC-REFRESH: brings the summaries of the pane up to date: the Knowledge Base folder,
           *> the model list and what each of the four group buttons holds.
           *> Uses:   the settings AGENT-1-ENTRY to AGENT-3-ENTRY, which the Agents dialog
           *>         (AGENTS-FORM, modal, closed just above) may have saved. It also reads the
           *>         application's model list and the key store.
           *> Result: It also asks CHAT-FORM, with INVOKE super::"PC-REFRESH"(), to run its own
           *>         PC-REFRESH (fire-and-forget: the chat runs it when its event loop is next
           *>         idle), so the chat follows the change. Lbl-AgentSum = how many of the three
           *>         agents are on; the [agent n] tags in Lst-Models follow the new choice; the
           *>         other summaries are rebuilt too. MODELS-FILE is first mirrored from the
           *>         application's model list (PC-SYNC-MODELS): records may be added, updated or
           *>         deleted.

           CALL    "PC-REFRESH"
]]></Event>
  </Control>
